EXECUTIVE SUMMARY:

This Zoning Map Amendment proposes to change the zone for one lot located east of Snyder Avenue and
south of West 31st Street. The applicant's site consists of three lots; the lot that is subject to this Zoning
Map Amendment is zoned MR-1 Medium-Density Residential-Established. The two adjacent lots to the
west and south of the subject site are zoned NB Neighborhood Business. The applicant is requesting to
change the lot zoned MR-1 to NB in order to provide consistent zoning across the site. This zone change
application was submitted in conjunction with an expedited preliminary plat application.

The applicant recently acquired the subject lot in order to make additional improvements-- a parking lot
to serve the abutting convenience store. As proposed, the existing house would be demolished and a
parking lot constructed. The subject lot is 3,600 square feet, with street frontage on West 31st Street. The
combined area of the other two lots is 9,765 square feet. These two lots have frontage on Snyder and
Randall Avenues and are developed with a 2,600 square foot convenience store and a canopied fuel
island. The proposed parking lot will provide 7 additional parking stalls. This gas station/ convenience
store has been a long-standing use and has existed in this location for over 50 years. The gas station is
situated in a neighborhood that contains a variety of uses, including numerous commercial uses along
Pershing, Snyder, and Randall.

Due to meeting the review criteria of section 2.2.1.d of the Cheyenne Unified Development
Code (UDC), staff recommends approval of the zone change, advancing it to the Governing
Body.
```

### Page 6 of 9

```text
4

ZONE CHANGE DATA:  In reviewing, providing comments, and making recommendations and decisions
on a proposed Zone Change Request, the Staff, Planning Commission and City Council shall use the
following criteria:

PLANCHEYENNE - The application is in accordance with the development policies and physical patterns
identified in the Comprehensive Plan.

Urban Residential Emphasis is the designation given to the subject area within ShapeCheyenne,
which has the future land use map within PlanCheyenne. Urban Residential areas are intended
for a variety of residential types, including single-family residences, duplexes, patio homes,
townhomes, condominiums, and apartments. Secondary uses include open spaces and
recreation, schools, places of worship, and other public or civic uses are encouraged. The NB
zone district can work within the Urban Residential area. NB has more restrictions on the uses
allowed and is intended to service the convenience shopping needs of a neighborhood. They are
characterized by a compact scale and pedestrian-friendly design that provides ease of access
from adjacent neighborhoods. PlanCheyenne supports enhancing and stabilizing existing
neighborhoods, and investment in this longstanding commercial business contributes to this goal.

SURROUNDING AREA - The application is compatible with nearby property, specifically considering existing
zoning, the Comprehensive Plan, and any other official plans and policies created under the guidance of
that plan for these areas.

The existing zoning is MR-1 Medium-Density Residential-Established. A designation of NB
Neighborhood Business would maintain consistency with the adjacent two lots. As previously
discussed, the NB Neighborhood Business zone district is able to fit within the context of the
Urban Residential future land use designation and is therefore compatible with the
comprehensive plan. In general, this neighborhood supports a wide variety of uses and a gas
station at this property is an appropriate use. This is proven by the fact that the gas station has
occupied the site for over 50 years.

ZONING: BASIC STANDARDS & USES - The suitability of the subject property for development according to
the standards and uses of the existing zoning district, compared to the suitability of the subject property
for development according to the standards and uses of the proposed zoning district;

The current zoning of MR-1 is typically not appropriate for commercial uses and is intended for
principally residential uses. The NB zoning already exists on this site and is appropriate for
commercial sites that are integrated into neighborhoods. The proposed parking lot and site
improvements of landscaping and pedestrian walkways are an upgrade to the property at a
highly visible intersection. As proposed, additional landscaping and trees will be provided along
all three street frontages. The proposed parking lot will also help relieve some of the current
congestion and circulation issues present on site. Under the proposed NB Neighborhood Business
zone district, the property would be able to be developed according to the standards of that
district as laid out by the Cheyenne UDC.
```

### Page 7 of 9

```text
5

STREETS & OPEN SPACE - The ability of the subject property and surrounding vicinity to be developed
according to the Subdivision Standards in Article 4 considering the proposed zoning;

The property should be able to be developed according to the standards in Section 4 of the UDC.
No new Right-of-Way is being proposed with this project. Open Space will be further evaluated at
the time of Site Plan review, at which time any requirements or exceptions thereto will be
determined. The street network in this area is very robust with small blocks and multiple
connections that accommodate a variety of uses and modes of transportation.

ZONING: INTENT, APPLICABILITY & DESIGN OBJECTIVES - The ability of the application to support the
Intent and Applicability statements of the proposed zoning district, and achieve the Design Objectives of
any specific standards.

The NB Neighborhood Business zone district is intended for Retail, Employment, Service and Civic
uses to support adjacent residential neighborhoods. This property would be able to meet that
intent within the context of an Urban Residential land use in the area.

ZONING: FUTURE DEVELOPMENT - The ability of all potential future development to meet all applicable
standards for development in the proposed zoning district, including other development options in the
event that any specific development proposed in association with the application is not executed after
approval.

This application is a zone change to consolidate the zoning across the subject site that is already
being used as a gas station and convenience store. The consolidation of the zoning removes the
uncertainty or potential confusion that may be caused by having residential zoning on a non-
residential use.

